{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "EnvironmentSync",
  "description": "When .env.local is saved, checks if mock or prod mode is active and verifies all required env vars, DynamoDB tables, AppSync endpoint, and Bedrock region are correctly configured — prevents missing-region and missing-table errors at demo time.",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "packages/dashboard/.env.local"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The file packages/dashboard/.env.local was just saved. Run the EnvironmentSync check:\n\n1. Read packages/dashboard/.env.local.\n\n2. Determine the active mode:\n   - MOCK mode: USE_MOCK_DATA=true OR DATA_MODE=MOCK (or both)\n   - PROD mode: USE_MOCK_DATA is absent/false AND DATA_MODE=PROD\n\n3. If MOCK mode is active:\n   - Check that these vars are present (values don't matter in mock mode, but they must exist for the app to start):\n     - AWS_REGION\n     - NEXTAUTH_URL\n     - NEXTAUTH_SECRET\n     - GITHUB_CLIENT_ID\n     - GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET\n   - Respond with a brief table showing which of those are set vs missing.\n   - End with: \"EnvironmentSync: DATA_MODE is MOCK — AWS connectivity checks skipped.\"\n   - Stop here.\n\n4. If PROD mode is active, check each of the following and build a results table:\n\n   **Core AWS**\n   - AWS_REGION is set and non-empty\n   - AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID is set and non-empty\n   - AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY is set and non-empty\n\n   **DynamoDB tables** (use AWS CLI: `aws dynamodb describe-table --table-name <TABLE> --region <AWS_REGION>`)\n   - SHELTER_TABLE is set → table exists and status is ACTIVE\n   - CHAT_TABLE is set → table exists and status is ACTIVE\n   - DONATIONS_TABLE is set → table exists and status is ACTIVE\n\n   **AppSync**\n   - NEXT_PUBLIC_APPSYNC_ENDPOINT is set and non-empty\n   - NEXT_PUBLIC_APPSYNC_API_KEY is set and non-empty\n\n   **Bedrock**\n   - BEDROCK_REGION is set and non-empty\n\n   **Auth**\n   - NEXTAUTH_URL is set\n   - NEXTAUTH_SECRET is set\n   - GITHUB_CLIENT_ID is set\n   - GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET is set\n\n   **db.ts region guard** — read packages/dashboard/src/lib/db.ts and confirm DynamoDBClient is initialized with an explicit region (e.g. `region: process.env['AWS_REGION'] ?? 'us-east-1'`)\n\n5. Report results in this format:\n\n**EnvironmentSync — PROD mode detected**\n\n| Check | Status | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| AWS_REGION | ✅/❌ | value or missing |\n| AWS credentials | ✅/❌ | present or missing |\n| SHELTER_TABLE exists | ✅/❌ | ACTIVE or error |\n| CHAT_TABLE exists | ✅/❌ | ACTIVE or error |\n| DONATIONS_TABLE exists | ✅/❌ | ACTIVE or error |\n| AppSync endpoint | ✅/❌ | set or missing |\n| AppSync API key | ✅/❌ | set or missing |\n| BEDROCK_REGION | ✅/❌ | value or missing |\n| Auth vars | ✅/❌ | all present or list missing |\n| db.ts explicit region | ✅/❌ | pass or fix snippet |\n\n6. For any failures:\n   - If a DynamoDB table is missing: remind the user to run `cd packages/infra && npx cdk deploy`\n   - If db.ts is missing the explicit region, show the correct snippet:\n     ```typescript\n     new DynamoDBClient({ region: process.env['AWS_REGION'] ?? 'us-east-1' })\n     ```\n   - Do NOT automatically edit any files — only report findings and suggested fixes.\n\n7. If all checks passed:\n   - Respond: \"EnvironmentSync: All checks passed ✅ — safe to run in PROD mode.\""
  }
}
